  "question": {
    "en": "9. Examiner correctly manages caregiver/child distress per the 'Managing Distress' protocol: (1) does NOT interrupt for distress when an interruption is not indicated (e.g., caregiver is managing child's upset, it is not escalating, child is not inconsolably or excessively distressed) and/or (2) initiates interruption per protocol in a timely manner when it is indicated (e.g., child is crying inconsolably and not responding to caregiver attempts to soothe, caregiver frustration is escalating to rough handling and/or threats of physical punishment). If no distress is displayed, score as '1.'"
  },
